{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"apivorous-loving-hyrax","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Observed on main: Mirror Guard scheduled run 32567576681 (2026-08-22T10:25:45Z) FAILED with:\n{\"check\": \"replication\", \"healthy\": false, \"reason\": \"GitHub main is behind/ahead of Gerrit main\", \"gerrit_sha\": \"8d9acfd27b...\", \"github_sha\": \"d6a2ea0d6c...\"}\nThe next scheduled run (32568260546, 10:41:14Z) passed — the mirror had converged. github_sha d6a2ea0d6c is the commit merged minutes earlier (change 2099); the \"lag\" was ordinary replication delay during a heavy merge burst.\n\nSymptom analysis (unverified leads, for Phase 1):\n- The replication check alarms on a single sample of Gerrit-vs-GitHub SHA divergence. During normal merge activity there is ALWAYS a window where the mirror trails; sampling inside that window is expected, self-healing lag — not an outage.\n- This is the same noise class as the push-warning ergonomics ruling already on record (bug 3ff9-a8f0, operator: \"suppress under normal load — noise, not outage signal\"): a red CI run on main primes agents/operators to investigate a non-issue.\n- Candidate remediation direction (to validate in Phase 1, not assume): tolerate expected lag — e.g. fail only when divergence persists across two consecutive samples, or when the divergence age exceeds a threshold derived from the replication SLO, or when GitHub is AHEAD (a true invariant breach) vs merely behind (expected lag). Which is grounded depends on the guard's documented intent — read the mirror_guard module + its introducing ticket first.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- [ ] Phase 1 determines the guard's authoritative contract (its introducing ticket/docs) and classifies this as defect vs working-as-designed. If working-as-designed, report back with the citation instead of changing behavior — the threshold choice is then an operator decision.\n- [ ] If a defect (single-sample alarm inconsistent with the guard's intent): fix RED->GREEN so expected transient lag does not fail the run, while a persistent or ahead-divergence still fails loudly.\n- [ ] caused_by attributed to the guard's originating ticket if the single-sample behavior shipped with it (scope-of-work attribution if an omission).\n- [ ] No weakening of the true-outage detection (divergence persisting, or GitHub ahead of Gerrit).","id":"5bd1-2343-ed83-40f0","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Mirror Guard replication check alarms on single-sample expected lag"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787400820490432001,"uuid":"34a669c8-1d12-4d92-aed6-f8071040ed75"}